ase  with involuntary manslaughter but just  in last few moments his lawyer has  released a statement they say this  decision distorts Helena Hutchins tragic  death and represents a terrible  miscarriage of Justice Mr Baldwin had no  reason to believe there was a live  bullet in the gun or anywhere on the  movie Set he relied on the professionals  with whom he worked who assured him that  the gun did not have live rounds we will  fight these charges and we will win so a  confident note from Alec Baldwin's  lawyer there just as a reminder of what  happened in October 2021 there was  rehearsals going on so this wasn't a  filming of the actual uh scene this was  a rehearsal inside a church set in New  Mexico you can see it there and Helena  Hutchins was filming as Alec Baldwin  pulled this prop gun out of a holster  now Alec Baldwin admits that he pulled  back the Hammer of the gun so that's the  back part of the gun but he's always  denied pulling the trigger and in fact  in interviews he's pointedly said that  he doesn't feel guilt over Helena  hutchin's death although he has  expressed his condolences to her husband  and son he has always denied pulling the  trigger what you see there this video  has been released by the Santa Fe County  Sheriff's Office and this is the  immediate aftermath  um of that incident as police try to  investigate what happened to 42 year old  Helena Hutchins a rising star in the  cinematography world and certainly  people I've been speaking to say that  they've been fighting for this criminal  accountability for Helena Hutchins death  they say they've had lawsuits have been  filed countersuits have been filed as  this game of blame and counter blame has  played out but this is the first step  towards any criminal Reckoning and the  family of Helena Hutchins have welcomed  this move they released a statement in  the wake of these charges being  announced they said we want to thank the  Santa Fe sheriff and the district  attorney for concluding their thorough  investigation and determining that  charges for involuntary manslaughter are  warranted for the killing of Helena  Hutchins with conscious disregard for  human life our independent investigation  also supports charges are warranted it's  a comfort to the family that in New  Mexico no one is above the law we  support the charges we'll fully  cooperate with this prosecution and  fervently hope the justice system works  to protect the public and hold  accountable those who break the law  in addition to these statements that  we've had from the Santa Fe District  Attorney's office and from Helena  Hutchins family Andrea Reeb who's a  special prosecutor in this case made the  note that if any one of these three  people so Alec Baldwin the armor of  Hannah Gutierrez read and also David  Halls the assistant director who's made  a plea deal in connection with this case  she said if any one of those three had  done their job Helena Hutchins would be  alive today it's that simple she also  noted that the evidence they've  collected shows a pattern of criminal  disregard for safety on the film set and  that is in accordance with what we heard  in the wake of this shooting from crew  members and in fact seven crew members  just the day before Helena Hutchins was  shot dead walked offset in protest over  what they viewed as a willful disregard  for the safety of cast and crew on set  so they're were warnings given in  advance of this and in fact that's  something that the district attorney has  drawn upon  um when she announced the charges  against Alec bald when she said he was  not only an actor on this set he was  also one of the producers and he was a  veteran actor she said and they say that  in in line with this investigation  they've spoken to many A-list actors who  have said that they regularly check the  guns on set even if they're prop guns  they check to see if they've got live  bullets in or they asked someone else to  do so that so the Santa Fe